/**
 * Course API Test Examples
 * Use with REST Client extension in VS Code or any HTTP client
 */

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@authToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
@courseId = 123e4567-e89b-12d3-a456-426614174000

### 1. Get All Courses (No Auth Required)
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses
Content-Type: application/json

### 2. Get Courses with Filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses?category=programming&level=beginner&page=1&limit=10
Content-Type: application/json

### 3. Search Courses
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses?search=javascript
Content-Type: application/json

### 4. Get Course Details
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses/{{courseId}}
Content-Type: application/json

### 5. Get Enrolled Courses (Auth Required)
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses/enrolled
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 6. Enroll in Course (Auth Required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/courses/{{courseId}}/enroll
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 7. Get Course Progress (Auth Required)
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses/{{courseId}}/progress
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 8. Get Courses - Pagination Test
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses?page=2&limit=5
Content-Type: application/json

### 9. Get Courses - Multiple Filters
GET {{baseUrl}}/courses?category=programming&level=intermediate&search=react&page=1&limit=20
Content-Type: application/json

### Expected Responses

